{
  "id": "pythagorean_theorem",
  "title": "Pythagorean Theorem",
  "description": "Verifying square corners using the Pythagorean theorem. Calculate the hypotenuse length C from sides A and B using the formula C = √(A² + B²).",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Pythagorean Theorem\n\nThe Pythagorean theorem is often used to verify if a corner is square (90 degrees).\n\n**Formula:** C² = A² + B²\n\nOr expressed as: C = √(A² + B²)\n\n## Example\nWith A = 5 m and B = 10 m, the hypotenuse C = √((5)² + (10)²) = √125 ≈ 11.2 m"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "sideA",
          "label": "Side A",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 5,
          "unit": "m"
        },
        {
          "id": "sideB",
          "label": "Side B",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "m"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "hypotenuse",
          "label": "Hypotenuse C",
          "formula": "Math.sqrt(inputs.sideA * inputs.sideA + inputs.sideB * inputs.sideB)",
          "unit": "m",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "squareA",
          "label": "A²",
          "formula": "inputs.sideA * inputs.sideA",
          "unit": "m²",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "squareB",
          "label": "B²",
          "formula": "inputs.sideB * inputs.sideB",
          "unit": "m²",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "sumSquares",
          "label": "A² + B²",
          "formula": "inputs.sideA * inputs.sideA + inputs.sideB * inputs.sideB",
          "unit": "m²",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Triangle Type",
        "Side A",
        "Side B",
        "Hypotenuse C",
        "Square Corner?"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Reference (3-4-5)",
          "3",
          "4",
          "5",
          "Yes (90°)"
        ],
        [
          "Example 1",
          "5",
          "10",
          "11.2",
          "Yes (90°)"
        ],
        [
          "Example 2",
          "6",
          "8",
          "10",
          "Yes (90°)"
        ],
        [
          "Example 3",
          "7",
          "9",
          "11.4",
          "Yes (90°)"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}